{"parentUuid":"fca5fb92-6316-485b-8242-3b7309bf59e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LVBHQtwoFMa8an8uE9ayo1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No MCP code in this directory. Since this is a learning plan (not an implementation task), I'll share it directly rather than using the plan file workflow.\n\n---\n\n## MCP Learning Plan — Advanced Track\n\n### 1. Protocol Foundations (refresh & deepen)\n\n- **Read the spec**: [modelcontextprotocol.io/specification](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification) — the canonical source. Focus on the JSON-RPC transport layer, capability negotiation, and lifecycle.\n- **Mental model**: MCP is a stdio/SSE JSON-RPC protocol with three primitives — **Tools** (functions the LLM can call), **Resources** (data the LLM can read), and **Prompts** (reusable prompt templates). Servers expose these; clients (Claude Code, Claude Desktop) consume them.\n- **Key concepts to nail down**: capability negotiation at `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, tool listing vs. invocation, resource URI schemes, sampling (server-initiated LLM calls).\n\n### 2. Audit Your Existing Servers\n\nYou already run several MCP servers (adam-mcp, ops-mcp, chrome-devtools, slack, server-memory, context7, handoff, nesso). Good learning exercise:\n- Read their configs in `~/.claude/settings.json` or `claude_desktop_config.json`\n- Trace one tool call end-to-end: client sends `tools/call` → server processes → returns result\n- Identify which servers use **stdio** vs **SSE** transport\n- Look at how `server-memory` implements entity/relation CRUD — it's a clean reference for stateful servers\n\n### 3. Build an MCP Server (Python — FastMCP)\n\nFastMCP is the fastest path from zero to working server:\n\n```\npip install fastmcp\n```\n\n**Suggested progression:**\n1. **Hello world** — single tool, stdio transport, register in Claude Code\n2. **Add resources** — expose a file or dataset as a resource with a URI scheme\n3. **Add prompts** — create a reusable prompt template\n4. **Stateful server** — maintain state across calls (like server-memory does)\n5. **SSE transport** — switch from stdio to HTTP/SSE for remote deployment\n\n**Reference**: You have the `mcp-builder` skill available — invoke `/mcp-builder` when you're ready to build and it will guide you through creating a production-quality server.\n\n### 4. Build an MCP Server (Node.js — `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`)\n\nSince you write JS primarily:\n```\nnpm install @modelcontextprotocol/sdk\n```\n\nSame progression as above but in your native stack. Compare the ergonomics with FastMCP.\n\n### 5. Advanced Patterns\n\n- **Composing servers** — how Claude Code aggregates tools from multiple servers\n- **Sampling** — letting the server call the LLM (bidirectional flow)\n- **Dynamic tool registration** — changing available tools at runtime\n- **Auth & security** — scoping what servers can do, secrets management\n- **Error handling** — structured errors vs. text errors, partial results\n- **Performance** — batching, streaming, connection lifecycle\n\n### 6. Architecture & Ecosystem\n\n- **Where MCP fits**: MCP vs. function calling vs. agent frameworks. MCP standardizes the *server* side; function calling is the *client* mechanism that invokes MCP tools.\n- **Ecosystem survey**: Browse [github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers) for community servers. Study 2-3 well-built ones for patterns.\n- **When NOT to use MCP**: Simple scripts, one-off integrations, or when a direct API call is simpler.\n\n### Suggested Order\n\n1 → 2 → 3 → 5 → 4 (if you want both stacks) → 6\n\nStart with the spec, then immediately audit what you already have — that grounds the theory. Building in Python first (FastMCP is more concise) lets you focus on the protocol, then reimplement in Node for depth.\n\n---\n\nWant me to save this somewhere (e.g., a docs file), or dive into any specific section?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":31476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CZhuFMwybnEnFUhHgY9RS","type":"assistant","uuid":"62a3ca3c-112c-449c-ae7e-096b501340d5","timestamp":"2026-04-04T01:58:04.108Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/theuser/Downloads/claude-session-fixtures","sessionId":"1c54dea3-2a8d-42ff-aeda-6f18bf4f4443","version":"2.1.92","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"ethereal-leaping-lollipop"}
